# Secrets, evidence, PII

- Never commit secrets. Use `.env.example` names only; values in `.env.local` (gitignored).
- Do not invent brand facts. Use MISSING / UNVERIFIED / VERIFIED.
- Label statements as FACT, ASSUMPTION, OBSERVATION, or RECOMMENDATION.
- Preserve sources/evidence metadata when available.
- Do not store real lead/PII data in Phase 1. PII must not enter prompts, logs, or global memory.
